concept :the_three_forms do
  name "The Three Forms"
  summary "The Three Forms is a cosmology and working model that describes coherent resonance as paths closing into stable figures."
  subkind :physical_system
  path "player/cosmology/the-three-forms.md"
  reviewed "2026-06-18"
  tags :resonance, :cosmology, :religion
  prominence :mythic
  registry true
  aka "the Trine", "the Triptych"
  function "Explains resonance as coherent paths closing into stable figures"
  nature "Cosmology and working model of resonance coherence"
  known_forms "Tetrahedron, Triangulum and False Form"
  operating_limit "The One Truth remains theoretical and has no known diagram"

  prose <<~PROSE
    The Three Forms is the oldest surviving way of thinking about #{ref :resonance, "resonance"} — older than the band-and-bandwidth model the #{ref :tuners, "Tuners"} work by, older, some say, than the ring. Its single claim is simple and strange: resonance is not formless. A vibration has a shape, and a vibration left to find its own way will try to close that shape into a figure. The figure it closes into is what it does.

    Most people meet the idea as a picture before they meet it as a theory. The Three Forms is drawn as a triptych — two figures of confident, lawful order flanking a third that the diagram itself marks as false. Tuners hang cheap printed versions over their benches. Scholars argue over the geometry. Devotional readers — the keepers of the #{ref :tessellan_communion, "Tessellan Communion"} chief among them — treat the three panels as a creed. The line written under every honest copy is the same: *Three forms, one conflict, one truth.*
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :how_it_works, heading: "The Closing of the Figure"
    A coherent resonance traces a path. The purer the coherence — the narrower the band, the truer the single wavelength — the more that path wants to return to where it began and close. A closed figure is stable: it braces itself, holds its frequency, and does reliable work. An open path bleeds, wanders, and fails. This is the whole of the model. Coherence is closure. To tune well is to help a vibration find its figure.

    Two figures dominate everything the system builds, because between them they cover what resonance is asked to do — to hold, and to move.

    **The Tetrahedron — the geometry of Form.** The figure of standing still: four faces bracing inward, the most stable close there is. This is the lawful shape of the **structural** band. When ringglass hardens a wall, the Three Forms says the stone is being coaxed toward the tetrahedral close — toward more form, more law, more of the quality the old panels label *light*, because a thing fully closed is a thing you can see clearly and trust. The Tetrahedron is gold in every drawing. It is the figure of the lattice, and the figure the ring itself was built to hold.

    **The Triangulum — the geometry of Will.** The figure of pushing: the smallest closed figure there is, and so the one that drives hardest. This is the lawful shape of the **kinetic** band — heat, motion, force. A #{ref :kite_sail, "kite"} under thrust, a refinery running hot, a current of unopposed motion: all of it, in this model, is resonance closing into the triangle and leaning forward. The Triangulum is red, the color of the work it does. Where the Tetrahedron holds, the Triangulum moves. Between Form and Will, the keepers say, sits everything that can be honestly made.

    The **signal** band is not given a figure of its own, and that absence is the heart of the cosmology. Signal is the path *between* the two lawful figures — the band along which a vibration is still deciding what to close into. Climb the coherence of a signal high enough, toward the single-wavelength horizon the #{ref :elves, "elves"} reached for, and the keepers hold that Form and Will stop being two figures and resolve into one: a single perfectly closed figure that holds and moves at once, with no waste and no bleed. They call it the One Truth, and no one alive has drawn it. It is the same horizon resonance scholars describe as perfect coherence — named as a destination rather than a limit.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :the_third_panel, heading: "The Figure That Will Not Close"
    The third panel of every complete triptych is the #{ref :the_false_form, "False Form"} — drawn as an impossible figure, a rhombus whose edges meet in ways no real edge can, shimmering where the other two are solid. It is the one path that returns to its beginning and yet does not close; the proof that contradicts itself; the figure that *is, and is not, all at once.*

    Almost everyone treats it as a teaching device. You draw the thing that cannot exist in order to show, by its violation, what coherence is — the way you learn a law fastest by seeing it broken. In common speech the False Form has thinned into an abstraction: falsehood itself, the lie that wears the shape of truth, the slow opening of any figure left untended. It is the most-drawn and least-believed of the three. See the #{ref :the_false_form, "False Form"} for the figure of speech it has become.

    The keepers insist the panel is not decoration, and they read the closing line as a warning rather than a flourish: *Order is not enough.* The two lawful figures, balanced, are still only order — a wall and an engine, holding and moving, and a system can be all of that and still be hollow. *Truth is more.* The One Truth is a thing beyond mere order, the figure the lawful two are reaching toward. *But falsehood is not.* Some houses of the #{ref :tessellan_communion, "Tessellan Communion"} therefore teach that the False Form has no being of its own. Others keep the same panel as a warning that a false closure can still exert force. Their disagreement determines whether the third figure may be sounded or only drawn.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :significance, heading: "A Question of Will"
    Whether the Three Forms are *forces* or *beings* is the oldest argument in the tradition, and it has never closed either. The plain reading is that they are principles — the way resonance behaves, no more willful than weather. But the older devotional readings speak of the figures as though they choose: the Tetrahedron *holding* the world, the Triangulum *driving* it, the False Form *pressing* against both. Most resonance scholars find the willful reading embarrassing and the principle reading sufficient. The keepers find the principle reading complacent. The triptych is content to show three figures and one conflict and leave the matter of whose conflict it is to the viewer.

    What is not in dispute is the smaller, stranger echo of the cosmology that walks around in daylight: the #{ref :fae, "fae"}, whose every waking hour is the work of holding a coherent figure against the pull toward the diffuse. A fae concentrating into a single clear shape, and bleeding back out into an occupied haze when the effort fails, is the closing of the figure made flesh — order held by will, at the scale of one person. The keepers point to the fae and say: this is the whole cosmos, in a body you can shake hands with. The fae, who have to live it, are generally less moved by the comparison.
  PROSE

  gm_note :appears, "Cheap printed triptychs hang over workshop benches, so a party waiting on a repair can read the panels off the wall. Gold marks the structural band and red the kinetic, which tells them what the machine in front of them does before its owner explains."
  gm_note :triggered_by, "Ask any working hand what a resonance device is doing and the answer comes back as figures closing rather than bands and " \
    "bandwidth, because the picture is what most people learned first. A #{ref :tuners, "Clarisant-trained Tuner"} corrects the framing and then uses it anyway."
  gm_note :complicates, "When someone in a scene calls a thing a false form, the phrase can mean the drawn third panel or the ordinary word for a lie that holds its shape. Keepers hear the first and speakers usually intend the second, so an insult can land as a doctrinal claim."
end

relate :rel_three_forms_derived_from_resonance, :derived_from, :the_three_forms, :resonance do
  prose "The Three Forms is, at bottom, a cosmology of #{ref :resonance, "resonance"} — the claim that a coherent vibration has a shape, and that to tune well is to help it close."
end
